From: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: complete off-channel requests during reset

Clearing an active scan or remain-on-channel request without notifying
mac80211 leaves its request active after L1 recovery. A later cancellation
cannot complete it because the driver's request has already been cleared.
Full restart also requires the hardware scan completion before reconfig.

Keep the MCU_RESET guards around hardware channel restoration, but always
notify mac80211 when the corresponding active request is completed. The
request pointers and existing mutex prevent duplicate completions.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 channel.c | 3 +--
 scan.c    | 3 +--
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/channel.c b/channel.c
--- a/channel.c
+++ b/channel.c
@@ -336,8 +336,7 @@ void mt76_roc_complete(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 	mt76_put_vif_phy_link(phy, phy->roc_vif, phy->roc_link);
 	phy->roc_vif = NULL;
 	phy->roc_link = NULL;
-	if (!test_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->phy.state))
-		ieee80211_remain_on_channel_expired(phy->hw);
+	ieee80211_remain_on_channel_expired(phy->hw);
 }
 
 void mt76_roc_complete_work(struct work_struct *work)
diff --git a/scan.c b/scan.c
--- a/scan.c
+++ b/scan.c
@@ -39,8 +39,7 @@ static void mt76_scan_complete(struct mt76_dev *dev, bool abort)
 	}
 	mt76_put_vif_phy_link(phy, dev->scan.vif, dev->scan.mlink);
 	memset(&dev->scan, 0, sizeof(dev->scan));
-	if (!test_bit(MT76_MCU_RESET, &dev->phy.state))
-		ieee80211_scan_completed(phy->hw, &info);
+	ieee80211_scan_completed(phy->hw, &info);
 }
 
 void mt76_abort_scan(struct mt76_dev *dev)
